--- body ---
## Context

Child of tickets/0205. Re-scoped 2026-06-05 to the review-is-CI model:
the management surface invokes the 0217 sandbox-runner once per roster
entry — it does NOT implement a protocol client. Containment is the
runner's OS sandbox (read-only mount, secrets denyRead, minimal env),
not capability grants. Adding a reviewer = adding a roster stanza
(another agnostic CLI + endpoint), not writing an adapter. Seats:
0207's CLI seat over {OpenRouter, llama-server}, plus the 0206 Copilot
forge bot (the one server-side, non-container member). The seats never
run tests; the orchestrator runs them and feeds results into each
seat's prompt context. Helpers are tool-named where they wrap one tool
(0205 naming exception); the umbrella skill itself is generic.

## Relevant files

- new: skills/reviewers/SKILL.md (umbrella; generic)
- scripts/seat-runner-prototype.sh (0217) — the contained runner this
  skill invokes per seat
- new: reviewer roster config (one place: seat = {agent_cmd, endpoint,
  model, kind, status advisory|required}; no secrets — credentials via
  BASH_ENV path, see 0207)
- skills/verify/SKILL.md — calls into this instead of inlining mechanics
- tickets/0206, tickets/0207, tickets/0217 — the reviewers and the runner

## Actions

1. `/reviewers list` — panel roster, each seat's kind, advisory/required
   status, trial progress (MRs observed / projects covered).
2. `/reviewers request <pr>` — for each roster seat, run the 0217
   seat-runner over the PR diff (container per seat); plus the 0206
   forge-bot request (the one non-container member).
3. `/reviewers harvest <pr>` — collect all seats' findings, normalize to
   the 0205 contract shape, emit one findings file for the gate.
   Unparseable findings are surfaced as WARN, never silently dropped
   (the prototype's normalizer leaks template-echo/dupes — tighten here).
4. `/reviewers scorecard <pr> <verdict-summary>` — append the per-MR
   trial line to the owning ticket's log, in a fixed schema (seat,
   finding-id, file:line, class TP|FP|FN, latency) so 0205's integration
   review is evidence-based, not vibes (operational-panel blocker).
5. Per-seat fail-open: one seat hanging/erroring WARNs and the gate
   proceeds on the rest — never ESCALATEs the whole verify run.
6. Config lives in one place (the roster); no secrets in config —
   credentials via BASH_ENV path (see 0207).

## Test

Shell test with a stub agnostic CLI on PATH + stubbed forge CLI:
`request` runs the 0217 runner once per configured seat; a seat that
attempts a repo write is blocked by the SANDBOX (0217 self-test);
`harvest` merges two stub finding files into one normalized output and
surfaces an unparseable finding as WARN; `scorecard` appends a valid
erg log line (verbs: created/note/closed only) that `erg validate`
accepts; one stubbed seat hang proves fail-open (gate proceeds).

## Exit criteria

- [x] /reviewers skill with list/request/harvest/scorecard, catalog-registered — PR #292; README.md catalog line present
- [x] request invokes the 0217 sandbox-runner per roster seat; per-seat fail-open proven — tests/test_reviewers.sh "bad seat fail-open WARN"
- [x] harvest normalizes to the contract shape; unparseable → WARN, never dropped — tested; hardened further by 0218/PR #298 (template-echo drop + dedup)
- [x] scorecard writes a fixed-schema trial line (evidence, not vibes) — erg-validated in tests
- [x] verify/SKILL.md carries a delegation stub pointing to /reviewers (the full panel-extension contract is 0205's deliverable, lands after this) — skills/verify/SKILL.md:216-220
- [x] Stubbed shell test green; make check green — 19/19 assertions, make check passes
